<http://data.silknow.org/object/ee72a49b-a65a-3552-9c88-7ac421116c75>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Linen, plain weave with embroidered repeating rows of chinoiserie and other motifs (insects, animals, floral slips, etc.) in silk. Edged with hand-knotted fringe along top left edge: \"John Stilwell Drawear at Ye Flaming Soord Rusill Street Covint Garden Remoove at Quartear-Day 2 ye (3?) Pidgins in halfe moone Street\". Fair condition. Yellow-brown discoloration, brown stains, small areas of loss to and unfinished embroidery."@en ;
